  "title": "Build the cross-project pattern matcher as a new binary `decl-patterns` in tools/decl_splitter/src/patterns.rs. \n\nThis should:\n1. Scan decls directories across multiple projects (forge_domain, forge_main, forge_app, pi agent)\n2. Parse each split decl file with `syn` to extract:\n   - All `use` statements (external crate names + paths)\n   - All `#[derive(...)]` attributes and which trait crates they come from\n   - All trait impls (`impl Trait for Type`) and which trait crates they reference\n   - All function signatures and which types they return/accept\n   - All type annotations and which crates those types belong to\n3. Build a \"pattern fingerprint\" per decl: a vector of `(CrateName, UsageKind)` tuples\n4. Group decls by isomorphic patterns \u2014 two decls are \"isomorphic\" if they use the same external crates in the same way (same set of `(crate, usage_kind)` pairs)\n5. Report:\n   - Which crate usage patterns are shared across projects (forge + pi)\n   - Most common crate usage patterns within each project\n   - \"Overlap score\": percentage of forge decls that have isomorphic patterns in pi agent\n\nThe UsageKind enum should include: Derive, ImportPath, TraitImpl, FunctionReturn, FieldType, MethodCall\n\nOutput to stdout as a structured report. Accept --decls-dirs for multiple dirs.",
  "workspace_id": 6692394623987231963,
